cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FlowMCP or its benchmark data, please cite it as below."
title: "FlowMCP: workflows as MCP tools — a six-condition benchmark of tool-surface design"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Green
    given-names: Peter
repository-code: "https://github.com/PeterGreenAppliedAI/FlowMCP"
date-released: 2026-07-31
version: 0.3.0
keywords:
  - Model Context Protocol
  - LLM agents
  - tool use
  - workflow compilation
  - benchmark
abstract: >-
  FlowMCP is an MCP server in which each tool is one declarative workflow
  executed by a deterministic engine. The repository includes a six-condition
  benchmark (facade, primitive surface, tool search, mixed surface, textual
  recipe, code mode) across ten self-hosted models — 610 runs executed, 440
  analyzed, raw data and transcripts committed — measuring how tool-surface
  design moves task specification, sequencing, and recurring execution into
  or out of inference.
